title: What each member shows
pid: 9dcb4d7e-6dd5-4b02-a677-9966ba798a46
body: |2-
  A member as such -- a forkee as such, or a forker-only or an
  indirect member (a forker as such) -- shows its content less what N
  contains or hides and less what a note the user owns, but the
  member, contains (=owned_notes_containing=), and, drawn editable, its
  own folders but a forks folder, the folders of what the user keeps
  elsewhere, of what N hides in it and, under a forker of N, of what it
  hides of N's content among them.
  The birth facts follow the roles in which the member stands
  (=forks_folder_member_roles= in =server/refresh/viewnodestats.rs=):
  =(forks in 2)= where it claims (where the folder reads no claims,
  where the graph says N forks it), =(forks out 2)= where the graph's
  warrant and a visible record say it forks N; a mutual carries both,
  a detached forkee and an indirect member neither (so an indirect
  member's heralds show no 'b' flag toward N). Its relRepo fact is N's
  record of the fork where it claims, else its own record of forking
  N; an indirect member has none. A relRepo request
  on a member claiming nothing is refused at validation
  (=is_forks_folder_member_claiming_nothing= in
  =server/from_text/buffer_to_viewnodes/validate_tree.rs=): its record
  is in its own file, or it has none with N.
